  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AECID-GARKUA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is based on the experience of Oxfam and Garkua in the Diffa region, and will be implemented in a spirit of complementarity with the other actors present in the area to ensure the continuity of activities. In the event of a deterioration in the context, community structures (complaints committees, village management committees, SCAP/RU) will carry out certain activities in collaboration with Oxfam and local authorities and opinion leaders: inclusive targeting, distributions, training of young people and women, etc.  Oxfam&apos;s remote monitoring procedures will be applied to organise regular monitoring with these structures. In addition, in theevent that the project areas are no longer accessible, awareness-raising campaigns on malnutrition prevention and protection issueswill be carried out via Bosso&apos;s community radio stations.The aim of this project is to contribute to the Spanish cooperation&apos;s response strategy and the Humanitarian Response Plan in Niger by meeting the priority needs of womenand men affected by the security andclimate crises, by improving food and nutritional security and strengthening people&apos;s ability to protect themselves in the Diffa region of Niger.Strengthening food and nutritional security and improving community protection in Niger.Translated with DeepL.com (free version)</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="11">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Association Nig&#xe9;rienne pour un</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Nigerien Association for Sustainable Development (ANDD Garkua) is a Nigerien non-profit, non-political and non-confessional NGOcreated by Order n &#xb0; 0154 / MISPD / ACR / DGAPJ / DLP of 24 February 2016. Garkua is present in six of the eight regions of Niger. It aims to promote the rights of grassroots communities.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
